503 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 60 0 R
/T (Root Cause Analysis: Line 17 attempted to branch to target label END. However, the label END: was never declared in the source code. During Pass 2, `encode_i_type_binary\(\)` checked `if target in labels`. Because `END` was absent from `labels`, it fell back to parsing `END` as a decimal immediate via `parse_immediate\(\)`, triggering Python's `int\('END'\)` conversion error. )
/E (Root Cause Analysis: Line 17 attempted to branch to target label END. However, the label END: was never declared in the source code. During Pass 2, `encode_i_type_binary\(\)` checked `if target in labels`. Because `END` was absent from `labels`, it fell back to parsing `END` as a decimal immediate via `parse_immediate\(\)`, triggering Python's `int\('END'\)` conversion error. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 60 0 R
/T (Resolution: The issue was resolved by explicitly defining `END: ADD $r0, $r0, $r0` in `programPro.asm`, ensuring the first pass populates `labels['END'] = 17`. )
/E (Resolution: The issue was resolved by explicitly defining `END: ADD $r0, $r0, $r0` in `programPro.asm`, ensuring the first pass populates `labels['END'] = 17`. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
